+
+## Voyage 10 — Surgical DOM on all filters; never call `render()` from toggle handlers
+
+The Voyage 9 fix correctly split `change`/`click` listeners but still called
+`render()` on filtered views (Active/Completed) inside both the `change` and
+`click` (happy-dom fallback) handlers.  `render()` replaces `todoList.innerHTML`,
+which detaches every `<li>` from the DOM.  The Cypress acceptance test holds a
+reference to a `<li>` (via `.first()`) and after `.click()` tries `cy.find()` on
+it —  if the `<li>` was replaced by `render()`, the reference is stale and
+Cypress raises the DOM-detachment error.
+
+Real-browser failures (3 acceptance tests failing):
+1. "complete all checkbox should update state when items are completed / cleared"
+   — toggle-all not checked because items could not be completed without detach.
+2. "should allow me to mark items as complete" — DOM detachment after click.
+3. "should allow me to un-mark items as complete" — DOM detachment after click.
+
+Fix: Replace `render()` calls in both the `change` handler and the `click`
+fallback handler with surgical DOM updates:
+- On `#/` (All): toggle the `completed` class in place (unchanged).
+- On `#/active` when completing: remove the `<li>` (it no longer matches).
+- On `#/completed` when un-completing: remove the `<li>` (no longer matches).
+- On `#/active` when un-completing or `#/completed` when completing: keep the
+  `<li>` and toggle the class (it still matches the filter).
+
+Always update derived UI (counts, clear-completed, toggle-all) after every
+change — this fixes the toggle-all state update on all filters.
+
+No plant-perturbation added.
\ No newline at end of file
